<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gimhae</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kimhae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gimhae is a city in South Gyeongsang province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, west of Busan near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakdong-river">Nakdong River</a>. It was the centre of Geumgwan Gaya, the leading state of the Gaya confederacy, whose founder Suro established it, according to tradition, in 42 CE. Its Daeseong-dong tombs and shell mounds are major sites of Gaya archaeology.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gimhae.jpg" alt="Gimhae" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rémi Cormier · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gimhae_west.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
